# Root .gitignore blanket-excludes *.pt/*.onnx/*.onnx.data ("keep training
# reproducible instead of committing weights blindly") — a sound policy for
# real-scale model weights. This directory's Phase 2A spike artifacts are a
# deliberate, narrow exception: they're tiny (~40KB checkpoint, ~36KB ONNX),
# and docs/repair/showboat-ml/ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md's acceptance test
# (rankerIntegration.test.ts) depends on the ONNX file existing to prove the
# pipeline works without requiring every contributor to stand up a Python +
# PyTorch environment just to run `npm test`. Reproduction commands are in
# README.md regardless. Not a precedent for committing real-scale weights —
# Phase 2C+ artifacts follow the root policy.
!artifacts/run1/checkpoint.pt
!artifacts/run1/showboat-ranker.onnx

# Phase 2C dataset generation output (all profiles, including smoke): fully
# reproducible from code + master seed in well under a minute (smoke) to a
# few hours (full) — see phase2c/gen_dataset_v3.ts and DATASET_DESIGN.md.
# Even smoke's tiny fixture is ~500KB of generated NDJSON; regenerating on
# demand (`npm run ranker:gen-smoke`) is cheaper than tracking it, and its
# determinism (byte-identical dataset_hash across runs) is exactly what
# makes that safe to rely on instead of committing the output.
phase2c/data/

# Phase 2D: same root policy as above (checkpoints/*.pt, artifact/*.onnx
# already covered by the root .gitignore's blanket rules). The parity
# fixture is additionally excluded here even though it's JSON, not a model
# file: it embeds 150 raw feature vectors derived from a checkpoint and is
# meaningless without the (uncommitted) .onnx file it was generated
# alongside -- regenerate both together via parity_fixture.py. The small
# metric-summary JSONs (phase2d_results.json, phase2d_test_results.json,
# phase2d_sanity_controls.json, MANIFEST.json) are NOT excluded -- they're
# the actual evidence backing TRAINING_REPORT.md/ABLATIONS.md and are cheap
# to track, same precedent as Phase 2C's perturbation_benchmark_results.json.
phase2d/results/artifact/parity_fixture.json

# Phase 2E (relational-architecture research): same root policy again.
# Checkpoints (*.pt) and ONNX exports are already covered by the root
# .gitignore's blanket rules; excluded here additionally are the cached
# dataset (a pure re-encoding of the uncommitted phase2c/data/baseline
# shards -- rebuild with `python phase2e/data.py`) and the parity fixtures
# (raw feature vectors + checkpoint-derived logits, meaningless without the
# uncommitted .onnx they were generated alongside). The metric-summary JSONs
# under phase2e/results/ ARE tracked -- they are the evidence behind the
# report, same precedent as Phase 2D.
phase2e/results/dataset.npz
phase2e/results/artifact/parity_fixture_*.json
